<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI15-QA1-CROSSHOST-EVIDENCE-GAP-WINDOWS>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI15-QA1-CROSSHOST-EVIDENCE-GAP-WINDOWS" ;
  triage:title "AI.15 Mac↔Windows physical peer-pair evidence not yet collected" ;
  triage:description "docs/plans/phase-ai/sprint-ai-15-windows-peer-smoke.md remains status: proposed with no attached readiness-record evidence artifact. Closure requires one physical macOS daemon and one physical Windows daemon to pass every AI.13 peer-pair case in both directions (same original ULID both hosts), Windows loopback-TCP local CLI/graft proof before and after peer testing, and no Windows alternate local listener/path in use, with doctor reports, listener inspection, sanitized logs, and just lint && just test from the exact tested commit on both systems. No code fix closes this — it is a physical-execution gap only, and per the permanent transport architecture (UDS mac/linux local-only, TCP loopback+cross-host+all-Windows-channels) this evidence run is what proves the Windows TCP path end-to-end. All AI.16-AI.20 local/code-level findings are independently closed and merged; this is the sole remaining item for AI.15." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "CROSSHOST-EVIDENCE" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
